{
  "id": "T7b_heldout_transitions",
  "title": "Held-out (enhanced) transitions of the repairs",
  "population": "BASE paired with FINAL[v]; G01: base cells improved on Q06",
  "unit": "base cell",
  "notes": [
    "E02 transitions of the same base cell (identical cohort, checked); G01 vs the E05 BASE reference (all-pass share of cells passing Q06 at baseline): difference in pp; joint Q06 / E02 transitions (X06): T7c.",
    "Denominator exclusions (methodology missingness rules; JSON key excluded): no unit is excluded in this table by R02 (base cell(s) outside the paired cohort); R03 (base cell(s) outside the paired cohort); G01 (improved cell(s) without a valid pair).",
    "BL01: Includes dense_la/00 (BL-01 tolerance convention: possible false FAIL verdicts; disclosure-bearing aggregate); sensitivity SA1 in T10.",
    "IC1: Q06 is in-sample for test_feedback and combined_feedback: their loops see the ParEval test verdict and stop when it passes (every stopped_tests_pass trajectory is a Q06 pass), so they optimise the endpoint; for static_feedback Q06 is out-of-sample (measured once in phase 2, never seen by the loop). The variants therefore differ in trigger and stop rules, not only in feedback content; test_feedback cannot regress on Q06 by construction.",
    "IC2: E02 is not an independent confirmation of Q06 gains: it counts build failures, and most E02 improvements are the same cells as the Q06 improvements; the held-out signal proper is the joint transition X06 (e.g. Q06 repaired but E02 still failing) and G01.",
    "IC3: G01 compares Q06-repaired cells (cells that failed at baseline and are harder) with cells that passed at baseline (E05 BASE); its differences mix cell difficulty with overfitting, and its cohorts differ per variant.",
    "IC6: static_feedback repair triggers are dominated by clang-tidy bugprone findings and, on MPI, by low-confidence hints (design document: no trustworthy static MPI tool exists); static_feedback results measure this frozen blocking-set configuration, not static analysis in general."
  ],
  "definitions": [
    {
      "ref": "BASE",
      "text": "BASE: the 1,980 base cells (pilot_002 396 + full_ext_001 1,584), iteration-0 artifacts (use: initial code quality)"
    },
    {
      "ref": "FINAL",
      "text": "FINAL: for variant v: per base cell the artifact of the trajectory's terminal iteration (== STEP[v][2]); for trajectories terminal at iteration 0 the final artifact IS the base artifact (use: repair outcome per strategy on the identical 1,980-cell cohort)"
    },
    {
      "ref": "R02 repair_success_rate",
      "text": "R02 repair_success_rate: numerator = improved cells; denominator = cells failing the endpoint at baseline; unit = base cell."
    },
    {
      "ref": "R03 regression_rate",
      "text": "R03 regression_rate: numerator = regressed cells; denominator = cells passing the endpoint at baseline; unit = base cell."
    },
    {
      "ref": "G01 heldout_robustness_of_repairs",
      "text": "G01 heldout_robustness_of_repairs: numerator = improved cells with final E02 all-pass; denominator = improved cells with >= 1 valid pair; unit = base cell."
    },
    {
      "ref": "E05 enhanced_all_pass_given_correctness_pass",
      "text": "E05 enhanced_all_pass_given_correctness_pass: numerator = E02 all-pass among correctness-pass artifacts; denominator = correctness-pass artifacts with >= 1 valid pair; unit = artifact."
    }
  ],
  "ci_note": "95% CI: nonparametric cluster bootstrap, percentile intervals, stratified by block (pilot benchmarks resampled among the 12 pilot benchmarks, full_ext among its 48); seed 20261017; cluster = benchmark; 2,000 replicates (descriptive, unadjusted)",
